WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.190
- Hey, guys, it's Justine,

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:04.440
and today, we have one of
the brand new iPad minis

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.840
that were just announced.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.570
I've had a few of these over the years

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.720
and it was always one
of my favorite devices

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.910
because of its size.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.500
I've been traveling a
lot for about 10 years,

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.920
so, having something that is portable

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.910
and easy to take with me,

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.960
I mean, now, I mostly use my phone.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.450
But for people who don't have phones

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.860
or for scenarios like smart homes

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.610
or people that are in restaurants

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.170
that are now switching to iPads,

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.600
there are so many other
scenarios for this thing

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.160
than just a media device.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.570
Obviously, it is an
incredible media device.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.400
But the iPad mini has a bunch of updates

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.610
from the previous version.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.320
I honestly thought that Apple
forgot about the iPad mini

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.540
until recently, it has made its revival

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.520
and it is here and we're
gonna check it out.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.460
This is the 256-gig WiFi
and cellular version.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.040
Obviously, they have it in both models

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.513
if you do just want a WiFi version.

00:00:49.513 --> 00:00:51.250
This is the Silver version.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.650
It also comes in a Space
Gray and the Rose Gold.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.500
It's still exciting every time

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.220
even if I know what is inside the box.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.690
So, the first thing
that you're gonna notice

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:08.083
is yes, it does have that
same look as the old models.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.950
What is so shocking to me

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:16.280
is if Apple released this
as a phone next year,

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.210
I would not even, I would
be like, all right, cool.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.240
I wouldn't even think twice.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.870
Like, this is a realistic size

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.430
that I feel like we would be
okay with if this was a phone.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:26.730
I wouldn't even be surprised.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:27.750
Like, hello?

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.780
I will take your call, Justine here.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.060
I think most people would be more shocked

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.070
that I answered my phone.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.730
I hardly ever talk on the phone.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.770
Most of the time, I'm texting

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.330
or, you can find me on Twitter.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.820
Okay, we've got our iPad.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.520
One thing that I think that
you guys are gonna notice

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.370
and I saw a lot of people
talking about online,

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:45.270
is this is the same
design as the old version.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.240
So the original iPad,

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.950
like, not much has
changed as far as looks.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:50.680
It sill has our Touch ID.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.590
Let's see what else is in the box.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.300
We've got all of our paperwork, as usual.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.440
Ah, look at this.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.810
This is something I
haven't seen in so long.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.330
A SIM card ejector.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.240
Am I being sarcastic?

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.210
That's for you to determine.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.910
Oh, little, teeny, tiny Apple stickers.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.720
And that seems to be all
of our reading material,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.820
something that should with every iPhone,

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.160
maybe in the future.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.853
12-watt charging brick.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.100
Lightning cable.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.610
And that, my friends, is
everything that is in the box.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.453
Ah, it's starting up.

00:02:26.624 --> 00:02:28.350
Look at this.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.070
Oh, my phone just said,

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.580
do you wanna set up your new iPad?

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:35.150
Yes, I do, iPhone, thank you.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.210
You know me so well.

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.610
So, the iPad mini has a 7.9-inch screen

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.460
and what's great about the new version

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.990
of the iPad mini is it also
has the True Tone display.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:47.110
I'm actually a huge fan of
True Tone display on my iPad

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:50.490
'cause I do a lot of reading
and emails on my iPad,

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.430
so it adjusts

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.450
to whatever lighting
conditions you're currently in

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:54.550
that's best for your eyes,

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:55.960
so that's something that I do leave on.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.300
I do tend to turn it off
when I'm on my laptop.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.770
Mostly because if I'm doing
any sort of color correction

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.150
in my videos or my photos,

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.650
I just like knowing that my
screen hasn't changed colors.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.620
But if I'm just reading or
doing anything like that,

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.570
I'm a huge fan.

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:09.320
Okay, we're gonna
continue setting this up.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.170
It's official, let's click.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.003
Yes.

00:03:12.003 --> 00:03:13.620
With the new A12 Bionic chip,

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.110
you're getting a performance boost,

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.370
so the performance is
boosted by three times

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.190
and the graphics, by nine.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:20.490
I would like to see a show of hands

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:23.530
of anyone who had watched by
Bob Ross painting tutorial

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:24.590
on the iPad Pro.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:25.950
If you did and you would like to see me

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:29.360
try to do a Bob Ross
tutorial on this iPad mini,

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.310
let me know because this
is really exciting news.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.910
The iPad mini now finally
has Apple Pencil support.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.860
Now, while it doesn't have
Apple Pencil 2 support,

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.480
it does support Apple Pencil 1,

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.130
and one of the main reasons for that,

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:46.110
the iPad Pro has the magnetic,
flat-edged Apple Pencil,

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.730
so that magnetically charges,

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.740
magnetically pairs just like this.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.520
That's it, it's magic.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.450
Since this is one of the older designs,

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.640
